WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:01.430
- Don't be hard on yourself

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.563
for rebounding when an animal dies.

00:00:03.563 --> 00:00:05.014
You know it's not like dating.

00:00:05.014 --> 00:00:08.082
You're allowed to try
to replace the thing.

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:12.019
A few years ago I ended up
getting a job in Los Angeles.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:14.675
We had our cats, Gidget and Enzo.

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:16.833
Gidget's like a sweet, calico cat.

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:19.503
A little thick, but it's all muscle.

00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:23.524
Enzo is a gray marbled,
super-affectionate cat.

00:00:23.524 --> 00:00:25.604
Within two weeks of being in the apartment

00:00:25.604 --> 00:00:27.738
I get a phone call and it's my girlfriend

00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:30.147
and she's just sobbing on the phone.

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:31.855
"Enzo's dead."

00:00:31.855 --> 00:00:34.191
My girlfriend watched the cat

00:00:34.191 --> 00:00:37.191
jump up onto the sill of this window

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:41.609
and Enzo fell nine stories to his death.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.956
I go back home to downtown L.A.

00:00:45.956 --> 00:00:50.063
I see my girlfriend
holding a bloody towel.

00:00:50.063 --> 00:00:52.794
All the sudden I hear some loud rap music

00:00:52.794 --> 00:00:54.180
and it's my friend Jimmy

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.596
and he rolls up in a totally
sick convertible Mustang.

00:00:58.596 --> 00:01:01.561
Long story short, Jimmy and
I have to sort of figure out

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:06.031
how we can dispose of my
really sweet dead cat.

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:08.482
Downtown Los Angeles has no yards.

00:01:08.482 --> 00:01:10.948
Even the park is full of cement.

00:01:10.948 --> 00:01:12.642
There is a moment where I'm like,

00:01:12.642 --> 00:01:15.491
could I bury it in Griffith Park?

00:01:15.491 --> 00:01:19.427
So we look for a vet that can
actually incinerate this body.

00:01:19.427 --> 00:01:20.632
We end up finding one

00:01:20.632 --> 00:01:23.479
and we show up in the
convertible, top down.

00:01:23.479 --> 00:01:26.361
I bring the cat in, and
the vet walks in and says,

00:01:26.361 --> 00:01:28.131
"Oh, how's Enzo doing?"

00:01:28.131 --> 00:01:30.318
And then I have to sort
of explain to the vet tech

00:01:30.318 --> 00:01:34.009
that the cat is in fact
dead inside of the towel.

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:35.811
The vet tech was super helpful

00:01:35.811 --> 00:01:37.123
and gave me lots of options.

00:01:37.123 --> 00:01:40.129
I could get Enzo's ashes in an urn.

00:01:40.129 --> 00:01:43.875
They were very accepting of all
payment types, it turns out.

00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:46.616
So I say, can you take
him and incinerate him?

00:01:46.616 --> 00:01:49.281
I don't need the ashes, I
don't need anything special.

00:01:49.281 --> 00:01:53.187
The vet tech politely takes
Enzo from me in the towel.

00:01:53.187 --> 00:01:55.715
As I'm leaving, walking out of the vet,

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.794
the vet tech emerges from the back.

00:01:57.794 --> 00:01:59.641
"Hey man, like, do you need this towel?"

00:01:59.641 --> 00:02:01.324
He's, like, dangling this towel

00:02:01.324 --> 00:02:03.491
that has cat blood all over it.

00:02:03.491 --> 00:02:07.514
I'm like, no please, no thank
you, leave me alone sir.

00:02:07.514 --> 00:02:09.657
Two days later it's the weekend.

00:02:09.657 --> 00:02:11.438
My girlfriend and I are grieving.

00:02:11.438 --> 00:02:14.271
We go to the desert to find peace.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.321
My girlfriend and I both see
a sign on the side of the road

00:02:19.321 --> 00:02:22.105
that says, "Yucca Valley Animal Shelter."

00:02:22.105 --> 00:02:23.779
We go to the animal shelter.

00:02:23.779 --> 00:02:25.326
They give us two options.

00:02:25.326 --> 00:02:28.076
One is this kind of old lady cat,

00:02:28.076 --> 00:02:30.019
missing some fur, a little cross-eyed.

00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:31.214
And the other cat they show us

00:02:31.214 --> 00:02:34.214
is this beautiful orange marbled cat

00:02:35.139 --> 00:02:38.007
and it looks exactly like Enzo.

00:02:38.007 --> 00:02:41.453
We drove it home and
we named him Loverboy.

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:44.515
And he's been our little
Loverboy ever since.

00:02:44.515 --> 00:02:46.617
(cats purring)

00:02:46.617 --> 00:02:49.367
(rhythmic music)

00:03:07.251 --> 00:03:08.467
(gentle whooshing)

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.639
(metal creaking)

